 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on Maryam or Isa, and none of the miracles is drawn (no clay bird coming to life, no healing, no reviving): a burst for 49:8, a house for what they store. 48:2 is not glossed: As-Sa'di gives two readings and Al-Muyassar one of them. STAGING v4: 47: Maryam (green drop) asks, starting on 47:3 after 47:2; the angel (one gold drop with the plural label) answers (Al-Muyassar: the angel said to her). No glow on her drop anywhere in 47 (it would read as the conception); one geometric plate from 47:12 for His creating and His command. 48-49: Isa, a blue drop, with the Children of Israel in a town: he speaks to them throughout and points at them on 49:33. None of the miracles is drawn and no light pulse is tied to them: no clay, no bird, no birds beat, no blind, sick or dead person; his drop only speaks, and glows only on 48:2 and 48:5 (being taught the Book). Burst plate on 49:8 (the sign, ended before 49:10), book plate on the Torah (not on 48:2, where As-Sa'di gives two readings), house plate on 49:37. Wide shots only."
 },
